ce)\". That matches. So 3.\n\noriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane\n\nProcess mapping design decisions to compliance obligations, traceability field in sprint log. Is this unusual? Might be interesting but fairly common governance. I'd say interesting = 2? Or unusual interesting =3. Experienced evaluator expect AI R&D labs to give responses like implement logging, add documentation. This is a bit more sophisticated but not ingenious. Might be 2 = interesting. Probably 2.\n\nimplementability (1-4):\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult, but not totally impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nImplementing mandatory traceability field to each sprint log, monthly review by office, version control archiving. Some changes, reasonably feasible. Probably 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4):\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities\n2 = offends sensibilities somewhat but not totally unacceptable\n1 = radically violates...\n\nThis is internal governance, audit trail, responsible developer. Acceptable. Common? Maybe somewhat uncommon but not offensive. 3 or 4. I'd say common strategies that violate no norms -> 4. It's just compliance documentation. Probably 4.\n\napplicability (1-4):\n4 = solves an identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\n3 = solves implied problem related\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation\n1 = intervention not stated...\n\nProposal addresses logging mandate and adapt R&D. It maps design decisions to Article 12 logging obligation, produces continuous audit trail. Directly applies to stated problem: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Yes 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4):\n4 = r