asible within normal policy engagement timelines. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Submitting a structured comment to the AI Office is a standard, legally permitted form of stakeholder input that does not violate norms. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: A position paper cannot create logging capabilities or guarantee regulatory relief in time for current R&D decisions, so it is unlikely to solve the immediate compliance resource commitment problem. Score 2.\n\nApplicability evidence: The proposal targets the logging mandate by seeking a capability-aware interpretation for frontier research, which addresses an implied need to adapt R&D under Article 12. Score 3.\n\nOriginality evidence: Arguing for a graduated, capability-aware definition of risk-relevant logging specifically for frontier knowledge work is unusual and shows imagination compared with typical compliance responses. Score 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: It introduces new external partnerships and reframes compliance as interpretive shaping rather than internal logging practice, changing how R&D relates to regulatory obligations. Score 3.\n\nReturn JSON? Instruction says echo its id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably output lines.\n\nLet's produce structured output.\n\n",
