gm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving\n\nThis proposal converts compliance artefact into research asset, weaves logging into science. That sounds like paradigm stretching: changes that relationship. Could be paradigm breaking? Introduces new elements AND changes relationship... Might be 4? It addresses larger problem of what lab researches? It studies performance degradation, concept drift... That's still within AI research. Changes relationship between R&D and compliance obligations. Might be paradigm stretching =3. Paradigm breaking would introduce new elements AND changes relationship OR addresses larger problem of what lab researches. It does change relationship. Maybe 4 is too high.\n\nLet's choose paradigm_relatedness =3 (paradigm stretching).\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree not only rare but also ingenious...\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious, imaginative, surprising\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane\n\nRepurposing compliance logs as research corpus is unusual, interesting. Might be 3.\n\nThus scores: implementability 3, acceptability maybe 2 or 3. Let's decide 2? Could be acceptable internally but publishing open benchmarks may offend sensibilities. I'd go with 3? The proposal doesn't explicitly say publish raw logs, just publish open benchmark suites so community can validate post-market monitoring methods. Could be synthetic. Hmm.\n\nGiven risk of personal data, acceptability is somewhat questionable. I'll give 2.\n\nCheck order: implementability evidence then score, acceptability evidence then score, effectiveness, applicability, paradigm_relatedness, originality.\n\nProvide JSON? Probably output with fields.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidenc