n. Maybe interesting? Common, mundane boring =1. Could be interesting =2. Probably common compliance pattern. So 1 = common, mundane, boring\n\nLet's assign:\n\nacceptability_evidence: The proposal uses immutable audit logs and cryptographic addressing consistent with EU AI Act traceability expectations and does not violate legal or sensibility norms.\nacceptability:4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building a write-once object store with query API per deployed instance requires new infrastructure but is a reasonably feasible engineering measure for an R&D lab.\nimplementability:3\n\neffectiveness_evidence: It provides automatic lifetime retention and indexed retrieval by time, input reference and verifier, directly covering the logging and traceability requirements in Article 12.\neffectiveness:4\n\napplicability_evidence: The store is designed specifically to meet the over-the-lifetime logging mandate for high-risk AI systems facing the stated compliance decision.\napplicability:4\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It introduces a dedicated log storage tool and deployment-time separation but still treats compliance as a logging practice rather than redefining R&D-compliance relationship.\nparadigm_relatedness:2\n\noriginality_evidence: Append-only lifetime log stores with cryptographic addressing are a common, well-known compliance pattern for regulated systems.\noriginality:1\n\nReturn JSON? Probably list.\n\nOutput format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Provide rating.\n\nLet's output nicely.\n\n",
